    "narrative": "The strength of our offense today centers on **Corbin Carroll** (76.75) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.74), both of whom benefit from highly favorable matchups. **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play, leveraging a prime #2 spot against the vulnerable Tidwell to maximize his stolen base potential, which remains our primary objective. Simultaneously, **Mickey Moniak** offers elite efficiency, as his matchup against G. Holmes creates a dynamic platoon edge that effectively mitigates any park-related concerns. **Seiya Suzuki** (72.88) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.28) round out the top of our production hierarchy, with **Seiya Suzuki** particularly well-positioned given his ability to exploit the slow delivery of Lowder to secure extra bases on the paths.\n\nBeyond the headliners, the lineup benefits from several targeted situational edges. **Brice Turang** (68.32) and **Jose Caballero** (67.40) provide the requisite speed profile to maintain our competitive edge in the SB category. **Jose Caballero** specifically overcomes a suboptimal #8 spot in the order thanks to a significant platoon advantage against the left-handed Sandoval. While **Josh Naylor** (50.84) maintains a starting role, we are exercising caution; he faces an elite arm in Cease, which drastically suppresses his projection and limits his ceiling. **Cole Young** (37.41) served as the closest call for inclusion, but he ultimately remained on the bench because he fell below our \"Zebras Floor\" of 40.0, as the combination of a tough matchup against Cease and a lack of elite speed made him a liability compared to our active roster.\n\nManagement of the remaining bench assets is straightforward today. Both **James Wood** and **Tyler Soderstrom** remain sidelined due to injury, leaving them unavailable for our rotation, while **Austin Riley** is out of the lineup entirely. We are maintaining **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Griffin Conine**, and **Edwin Arroyo** in reserve as we monitor late-breaking lineup changes across the league. No major weather concerns have been flagged for today's slate, but users should keep a close eye on any last-minute defensive adjustments that could shift the batting order for **Gabriel Moreno** or **Isaac Paredes**, as their current scores are highly sensitive to their projected spots in the lineup.",
